  "body": "**Description:**\r\n\r\n`SYNAPSE_LOG_LEVEL` is used in [`docker/conf/log.config`](https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/70f0ffd2fcd815a065b4734ac606654a2e11dd28/docker/conf/log.config#L44) to set the logger severity level but is not documented anywhere. \r\n\r\nThe log severity can also be overriden by setting a `log_config` in `homeserver.yaml` (`SYNAPSE_CONFIG_PATH`)\r\n\r\n> `SYNAPSE_CONFIG_PATH`: path to the file to be generated. Defaults to `<SYNAPSE_CONFIG_DIR>/homeserver.yaml`.\r\n\r\n\r\n### Dev notes\r\n\r\n - `SYNAPSE_LOG_LEVEL` was first introduceded in https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/commit/4f2e898c29de5b51e8c5893afa64e5b43d25048f\r\n - Changed a bit in https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/pull/5547/files\r\n - Someone noted as broken in https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/issues/6194 and maybe fixed in https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/pull/6197 \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n ### Alternative\r\n \r\n Remove this config altogether in favor of having to specify a `log_config` in `homeserver.yaml`\r\n \r\n \r\n ### Definition of done\r\n \r\n We have a nice list of variables on https://hub.docker.com/r/matrixdotorg/synapse which this would fit nicely in.\r\n \r\n  - [ ] Document `SYNAPSE_LOG_LEVEL` in [`docker/README.md`](https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/70f0ffd2fcd815a065b4734ac606654a2e11dd28/docker/README.md)\r\n",
